      {
        "id": 120215,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-07T17:00:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Actually, I'm a big fan of the Shadowrun setting.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=9\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\">  I played the game years ago, but haven't made an opportunity to play the newer versions (where they've apparently fixed a lot of the issues the earlier versions had).</p>\n<p>We did talk through the use of Karma and how a character can be upgraded, but it felt arbitrary. The game didn't really feel very playable without it - one of the thoughts we had was to just start with an upgrade or two to help make the game playable, but that didn't feel like a good approach to me.</p>\n<p>Who knows - I might try it again. But with all the games&nbsp;that are out there (and that are coming) that I already know I enjoy, it just doesn't seem like it's worth the time to me to play a game that's potentially not going to be enjoyable.</p>\n<p>But I'm pretty picky about what I'll spend time on.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>\n<p>I hope you really enjoy the game!  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/+1.png?v=9\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\"> &nbsp;And if not, I hope you at least enjoy spending time with the friends you are playing with.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/innocent.png?v=9\" title=\":innocent:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":innocent:\"></p>",
